{"title":"1984 AHSME Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The largest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/f/1ef11893ec3ad4dc6ce41ab6486489493eed2685.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{200}&lt;5^{300}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"84\" height=\"15\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/a/efa866cb535638fc856d7ddaa3b87eb8d3e54698.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }8 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }9 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } 10 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }11 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since both sides are positive, we can take the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09e23c13054c41bec0380a133491e0db995ec2da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100th$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> root of both sides to find the largest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87adf683f8e8940a1dbec4db6450c29c24c3dff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2&lt;5^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" />. Fortunately, this is simple to evaluate: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3a3f26200911534c37a95b55a5baba4d3d4a113.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^3=125$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"67\" height=\"15\" />, and the largest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perfect_square\" title=\"Perfect square\">square</a> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b829a6f0810a25e9ca9f85d690f2bafd0f2c1773.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$125$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/156cd79ea223ee199654928a5d473c77e7e4b96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11^2=121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />, so the largest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25c5023e520fb41b2015052644d693cd2e51302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11, \\boxed{\\text{D}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AHSME\" t